  "details": "<p>The thermopolium\u00a0was a public establishment, often interpreted as a sort of 'snack-bar', in the Roman world. These establishments served drinks and hot foods, usually at the lunchtime meal (<em>prandium</em>). There are 89 such establishments known in Pompeii.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The house and thermopolium of Vetutius Placidus (I,8,8) opens directly onto the south side of the Via dell'Abbondanza.",
